1.  I have never ever lost an intrinsic to a gremlin.  They have four
attacks, right?  It's the last attack that needs to hit you to lose an
intrinsic and there is only a small chance of it happening even if it
hits.  Plus, it has to be past midnight *and* they have to be hostile
in the first place.  Throw those rings in.

2.  Why not, they are not worth the scroll of charging.  I'm not
entirely sure if you will get more empty wands this way.

3.  Slow monster is useless.  Speed Monster and Make Invisible are good
for yourself and pets and that is it.  Speed Monster is semi-useful if
you lose your intrinsic speed to a shade in Orcus Town.

4.  If you want a different kind of food then yes.

5.  Iron golems are the worst I think, from iron items (weapons and
armor).  Have poison resistance and kill them from a distance.

6.  Well ... if you echant that elven stuff to +7 it is considered
magicial and will poly into more magic stuff like CoMR, BoWW and so
forth.  Unenchanted they are not really worth it unless you really need
a T-Shirt.

7.  Polying spell books is not the best idea because each book can be
read only 4 times and each poly increments that invisible counter once.
 Poly them too many times and you get books of blank paper, or a book
you can only read once.

8.  In my experience items with negative bonuses produce items with
negative bonuses.  Is that what you want?

9.  I would poly the cursed rings but not the armor, because rings are
more useful generally.  A cursed chain mail is only going to get you
some non-magical armor that probably has negative bonuses.

Ok, good luck.



